Baritone runs its searches and rescans on a private, unbounded, non-daemon pool, and parks two never-ending cache loops (region packer, periodic save) in it. The host now supplies the executor (HostEnvironment.executor(): bounded, named, daemon) and the two long-lived loops get their own daemon threads, so they cannot occupy a slot of the bounded pool.

